    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8b4bba23-7243-55e3-8b30-b7d71a009323",
      ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{28}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3.$\n\n${g}^{\u2032}(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{28}{3}\\sqrt{x}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{14}{3}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
